From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:53:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] sync: Stop replaying in-flight actions on reconnect

Rebuilding the reconnect queue from every retained request also replays
actions whose responses were lost. The server may already have executed
those actions, so replay can repeat external side effects.

Fail handed-off actions with an ordinary FunctionResult error and remove
them from the replay set. Preserve actions still in the base client's
outgoing queue: they have never reached the transport and remain safe to
send, including after multiple interrupted reconnect drains. Use the
existing queue to identify them instead of adding a second send-state
machine. Retain the existing mutation replay and query restoration paths.

Document the handoff boundary for BaseConvexClient callers. Add focused
regressions for uncertain actions, repeated reconnects before and after
handoff, retained completed results, and continued mutation/query progress.
Update the maintained patch description and link upstream proposal #18.

Validation: rustfmt and git diff --check pass. The focused Cargo test was
blocked before compilation by the local disk reserve guard.
